          "docPath": "oss/javascript/langgraph/human-in-the-loop",
          "chunkIndex": 32,
          "score": 0.11876153208940043,
          "content": "When execution resumes (after you provide the requested input), the runtime restarts the entire node from the beginning—it does not resume from the exact line where [`interrupt`](https://reference.langchain.com/javascript/langchain-langgraph/index/interrupt) was called. This means any code that ran before the [`interrupt`](https://reference.langchain.com/javascript/langchain-langgraph/index/interrupt) will execute again. Because of this, there's a few important rules to follow when working with interrupts to ensure they behave as expected.\n\n### Do not wrap `interrupt` calls in try/catch",
          "rank": 19
