        {
          "docPath": "oss/javascript/langgraph/graph-api",
          "chunkIndex": 51,
          "score": 0.280083324956969,
          "content": "To support this design pattern, LangGraph supports returning [`Send`](https://reference.langchain.com/javascript/langchain-langgraph/index/Send) objects from conditional edges. `Send` takes two arguments: first is the name of the node, and second is the state to pass to that node.\n\n```typescript theme={\"theme\":{\"light\":\"catppuccin-latte\",\"dark\":\"catppuccin-mocha\"}}\nimport { Send } from \"@langchain/langgraph\";\n\ngraph.addConditionalEdges(\"nodeA\", (state) => {\n  return state.subjects.map(\n    (subject) => new Send(\"generateJoke\", { subject })\n  );\n});\n```\n\n## `Command`\n\n[`Command`](https://reference.langchain.com/javascript/langchain-langgraph/index/Command) is a versatile primitive for controlling graph execution. It accepts four parameters:",
